  <div class="tips-block">
    <h3>Pro Tips for Dehydrator Beef Jerky</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Preheat the dehydrator</strong> for 10 minutes before loading to ensure trays are at temperature from the start.</li>
      <li><strong>Add curing salt</strong> (Prague Powder No. 1) at 1/4 tsp per 5 lbs to extend shelf life and improve food safety.</li>
      <li><strong>Blot surface oil</strong> from finished strips immediately — oil speeds rancidity.</li>
      <li><strong>Don't crowd the trays</strong> — overlapping strips don't dry evenly and can stay moist in the center.</li>
      <li><strong>Know your storage window.</strong> Uncured homemade jerky keeps 1–2 weeks at room temperature — see <a href="/guides/how-long-does-beef-jerky-last/">how long beef jerky lasts unrefrigerated</a> for the full breakdown by cure and container.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
